# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FULL LOCAL DEV — no GitHub / Supabase / Ably accounts required.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#   bun run db:up && bun run db:migrate    # local Postgres (once)
#   bun run dev:web                        # UI + API against local DB, no login
#
# This runs the whole web app + API + database locally. Auth is BYPASSED: because
# no Supabase env is set below, the API treats you as the fixed dev user in
# OPENREMOTE_DEV_AUTH_SUBJECT, and the UI's login gate is satisfied by /api/me —
# so you never hit a GitHub sign-in.
#
# For the agent/host side (browser ↔ host), use `bun run dev` (relay + mock host)
# — see CONTRIBUTING.md. This file is just the web/API/DB layer.
#
# .env.local is gitignored — safe to keep your own copy here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ---- Local Postgres (from `bun run db:up`) ----
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/openremote

# ---- Dev auth bypass (NEVER set these in production) ----
# A FIXED uuid so "your" local user + hosts persist across restarts. Any uuid works.
OPENREMOTE_DEV_AUTH_SUBJECT=00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
OPENREMOTE_DEV_AUTH_EMAIL=dev@local

# ---- Transport: local relay WebSocket (no Ably needed) ----
NEXT_PUBLIC_TRANSPORT=ws
NEXT_PUBLIC_RELAY_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8787

# ---- Leave Supabase BLANK ----
# The dev-auth bypass only kicks in when Supabase is unconfigured. Setting these
# would force real GitHub login. Leave them empty for zero-auth local dev.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
